  "changes": [
    {
      "id": "weekly-upstream-20261101",
      "notes": "Portable none maps to low with compatibility warning using the exact published model regexp, preserving Grok4.20, future multi-digit-major and suffix boundaries; exact grok-4.6 alone maps portable xhigh/max to xhigh, other models fall back to high. Explicit provider overrides remain untouched. Shared canonical Responses engine deduplicates citations repeated by final output_item.done and emits missing text/citations for completion-only or announced-without-delta message items; xAI-specific fallback preserves other provider namespaces. Native apiKeyProvider resolves fresh authentication for Responses, preserved legacy Chat, files, batch, image, speech, transcription, video/polls and realtime client-secret requests; WS streaming transcription resolves fresh headers at connect with case-insensitive override precedence and no placeholders. configureXAIChat installs owning reasoning policy on reusable compatible engine so OpenAI reasoning mapping does not alter the xAI request first. Reviewed upstream: @ai-sdk/xai 5.0.30 to 5.0.35. Validation passed: node Scripts/test-packages.mjs (all 52 owning package suites and the compatibility facade); node Scripts/sdk.mjs generate --check; node --test Scripts/tests/*.test.cjs (27 passed); docs-site check and build (100 pages). Live provider calls were not run.",
      "compatibility": "Minor release for additive native API; existing static settings and call sites remain compatible. Updated direct dependency minimums are recorded in the manifest. Existing documented JS/framework and native product gaps remain; version-delta review does not imply full parity or live-service testing. Explicit custom authentication skips an unused credential supplier, a deliberate native callback-order adaptation."
    }
  ],
